k biceps  and shoulders so each muscle group works  two times a week and then you have one  day a full rest on day one for the abs  for the chest and for the triceps you'll  do the following for the apps one minute  of two up and one down now just remember  if you can't make a full minute it's  fine to rest a few seconds in between  you will get to a full minute when you  are stronger now if you can't make a  full minute it's fine to rest a few  seconds in between you will get to a  full minute when you are stronger next  is one minute of seated ab circles on  each side when you are stronger you will  do it while hanging  third one minute twisted mountain  climbers fourth 30-minute starfish  crunches and then you rest for 30  seconds number five one minute scissors  and then lastly for the abs it's one  minute knee tucks now let's move on to  the chest workouts first normal bench  press now this is important so listen up  set your weight heavy enough so that you  can barely reach 10 repetitions on your  first set you will do a total of four  sets so the aim is to do every set until  muscle failure and after the bench press  you move on to the incline bench press  and next you can choose either you can  do normal dips or you can do lower cable  cross over now these three exercises  you've worked on your lower chest your  middle chest and your upper chest for  the triceps you will do the barbell  tricep extensions while laying down on a  bench and then lastly tricep rope push  downs now this workout should only take  you around one hour if it takes a lot  longer then you're resting too long  between your sets and then to finish  this workout you'll do four normal sets  of traditional push-ups each set until  failure and after this  your body will know that it just had a  killer workout let's move on to day two  day two is legs and abs first up abs  number one jack knives with weights on  your feet and head until failure next up  one minute marching planks number three  scissors with sit-ups you do this for 30  seconds and then  rest for 30 seconds and then you go  again then it's bicycles with weight but  do it slow with your feet up off the  ground do the one side fully before you  do the other side and you do this until  failure next up is weighted ab crunches  and lastly is the hanging leg lifts  until failure and that's it for the app  so let's move on to the legs first up is  squats remember four sets for all the  exercises with barely reaching 10 reps  with the first set after the squats it's  walking lunges  and then a hamstring curls  and after the hamstring curls it's time  for standing cuff raises now a lot of  people also include leg extensions here  but i would not recommend this because  it's really tough it's really hard on  your knees especially if you had a knee  injury so to finish the leg workout i  would usually do the leg press machine  slowly or deadlifts all right let's move  on to day three which is your back your  biceps and shoulders let's start with  the back first you can do wide grip pull  downs and then when you're stronger you  can do normal pull ups when you're done  normal face pulls with the rope and then  hyper extensions for your lower back and  then number four  seated cable rows  after that you'll move on to the biceps  and you're gonna do normal chin ups  first  and if you're not strong enough you can  do normal bicep curls with the curl bar  and then you move to rope bicep curls  for the shoulders you're gonna do  overhead press with dumbbells and then  lastly front and side lateral shoulder  raises and then on day four you're gonna  do the same workout routine as you did  on day one day five the same as day two  and day six the same as day three and on  day seven you're gonna rest now remember  for the weight training exercises you  need to give it your all in every single  set and you need to remember to add the  weights as soon as you get stronger well  if you give it your all and barely reach  10 repetitions with your first set then  you know the weight is fine but as soon  as you can do more than 10 reps then you  know the weight is too light for you and  your muscles need more resistance so you  need to add some weights then you just  do the rest of the sets until failure  but if you can barely reach six  repetitions then it is probably too  heavy for you so then you just have to  adjust the weights to make it a little  bit lighter now don't try to show off to  the people in the gym or try to cheat  the workouts  leave your ego at home when you come to  the gym focus on your form doing every  set the right way now the workout is  just a small part of getting bigger  muscles if you don't eat right you're  not gonna see the gains that you want to  see so in the next video i'm gonna share  my full nutritional plan with you so  if you haven't yet subscribe so you  won't miss that video and that's it guys  cheers
 

